## DATA LAYER — HOOKS

**Every hook follows this exact contract — no exceptions:**

```js
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

export function useKPIs() {
  const [data, setData]       = useState(null);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [error, setError]     = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetch('/data/kpis.json')
      .then(r => { if (!r.ok) throw new Error('kpis.json not found'); return r.json(); })
      .then(d => { setData(d); setLoading(false); })
      .catch(e => { setError(e.message); setLoading(false); });
  }, []);

  return { data, loading, error };
}
```

**All seven hooks:**

| Hook | Fetches | Returns |
|---|---|---|
| `useContract.js` | `/data/frontend_contract.json` | `{ contract, loading, error }` |
| `useKPIs.js` | `/data/kpis.json` | `{ data, loading, error }` |
| `useCharts.js` | `/data/charts.json` | `{ charts, loading, error }` |
| `useInsights.js` | `/data/insights.json` | `{ insights, loading, error }` |
| `useTiers.js` | `/data/influencer_tiers.json` | `{ tiers, loading, error }` |
| `usePlatforms.js` | `/data/platform_performance.json` | `{ platforms, loading, error }` |
| `useForecast.js` | POSTs to `/api` | `{ predict, result, loading, error }` |

**useForecast.js specific rules:**
- Exposes `predict(inputObj)` function, NOT a useEffect
- Calls `fetch('/api', { method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type':'application/json'}, body: JSON.stringify(inputs) })`
- **NEVER uses `import.meta.env.VITE_WORKER_URL`** — relative `/api` always
- `loading` starts `false`, becomes `true` during prediction, back to `false` when done
- Clears `error` on each new predict call

